<h3 id="calculations">Calculations</h3>
<p>Net ROA (Post-Tax) is calculated as follows:</p>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Net ROA</strong> = (<strong>Gross ROA</strong> - <strong>Property Tax</strong>) * (1 - <strong>Rental Income Tax Rate</strong>).</li>
</ol>

<p>For instance, for New York City in 2019 (City Centre):</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Gross ROA:</strong> 5.83%</li>
  <li><strong>Property Tax:</strong> 0.88%</li>
  <li><strong>Rental Income Tax:</strong> (5.83% - 0.88%) * 15% = 0.7455%</li>
  <li><strong>Net ROA:</strong> (5.83% - 0.88%) * (1 - 0.15) ≈ 4.22%</li>
</ul>

<p>Bond Yield (Post-Tax) is calculated as follows:</p>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Bond Yield (Post-Tax)</strong> = <strong>Bond Yield</strong> * (1 - <strong>Tax Rate</strong>).</li>
</ol>

<p>For instance, for U.S. 10-Year Bond Yield in 2019:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Bond Yield:</strong> 2.00%</li>
  <li><strong>Tax Rate:</strong> 15%</li>
  <li><strong>Bond Yield (Post-Tax):</strong> 2.00% * (1 - 0.15) = 1.70%</li>
</ul>

